td>MTF-Eta-1</td> <td>Birdbrains</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3095">SCP-3095</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-2</td> <td>Buyer Beware</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1808">SCP-1808</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces#eta-4">MTF-Eta-4</a></td> <td>Begone Thoth</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/bird">Team Bird Hub</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/join-the-flock">Join the Flock</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/spc-507">SPC-507</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3570">EE-3570</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-sacred-djehuti">The Sacred Djehuti</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/avian-anthology-i">Avian Anthology I</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/avian-anthology-ii">Avian Anthology II</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4688">SCP-4688</a></td> <td>A unit of intelligent <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3095">SCP-3095</a>-affected seabirds. Eta-4 specializes in information collection and analysis, field research, complementary field support, and in extreme cases, airborne combat. The task force was ultimately charged with protecting humanity after the BE-Class &quot;Migration&quot; End-of-Consciousness Scenario.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces#eta-5">MTF-Eta-5</a></td> <td>Jäeger Bombers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2764">SCP-2764</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/lte-2712-bosch">LTE-2712-Bosch</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/animalia">Animalia</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5514">SCP-5514</a></td> <td>A rapid-response unit specializing in the tracking, capturing, and containment of Large-Scale Aggressors (entities over 30m in height). Deploys from, and detains LSAs within Dimensional-Site-172.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-6</td> <td>Awareness Filters</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1504">SCP-1504</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-6</td> <td><span style="color: red">Presented</span> <span style="color: green">In</span> <span style="color: blue">Color</span></td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5020">SCP-5020</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5599">SCP-5599</a></td> <td>Investigation of <a target="_blank" href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/arcadia-hub">GoI-078</a> (<span style="color: purple">Arcadia</span>) and the recovery of associated anomalies.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-7</td> <td>Creepy Crawlies</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-363">SCP-363</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-9</td> <td>Maul Security</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1627">SCP-1627</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces#eta-10">MTF-Eta-10</a></td> <td>See No Evil</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2140">SCP-2140</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2136">SCP-2136</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1561">SCP-1561</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-125">SCP-125</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-020">SCP-020</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-904">SCP-904</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-571">SCP-571</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3519">SCP-3519</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/experiment-log-t-98816-oc108-682">Experiment Log T-98816-OC108/682</a>,<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3301-testing-log">SCP-3301 Testing Log</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3393">SCP-3393</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4879">SCP-4879</a></td> <td>Specializes in the investigation, acquisition, and initial containment of objects or entities exhibiting visual cognitohazards, visual memetic agents, or otherwise require indirect or alternative observation in order to safely handle.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-10-LatAm</td> <td>No los veo</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2155">SCP-2155</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces#eta-11">MTF-Eta-11</a></td> <td>Savage Beasts</td> <td>See <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces">this page</a> for information about this particular task force.</td> <td>Specializes in the investigation, acquisition, and containment of auditory and musical anomalies, including any auditory cognitohazards or sound-based anomalous threats.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Eta-11</td> <td>Snake Oil</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/a-world-s-legacy">A World's Legacy</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-12</td> <td>Dead Ringer</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/log-of-anomalous-items-vol-ii">Log Of Anomalous Items, Vol II</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-13</td> <td>Gulliver's Tourists</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2344">SCP-2344</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/wayfarers-hub">Wayfarers tale series</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3301-testing-log">SCP-3301 Testing Log</a></td> <td>Created to journey into a massive series of tunnels extending through extra-dimensional space, colloquially known as &quot;The Gate&quot;.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-30</td> <td>A Special Pest Control</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4713">SCP-4713</a></td> <td>A MTF squadron located in Poland to contain any animal-related anomalies.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-33</td> <td>Don't Have A Cow, Man</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3739">SCP-3739</a></td> <td>Post-<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/broken-masquerade-hub">Broken Masquerade</a> MTF assigned to subdue anomalous disturbances in rural areas. Contrary to the name, bovine anomalies are not their specialty; though, they are on standby when necessary.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Eta-73</td> <td>Trekkie's Tale</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4413">SCP-4413</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force charged with working with PoI-MP54 to undo e