www.scpwiki.com/task-forces">this page</a> for information about this particular task force.</td> <td>Specializes in tracking, containing, and exterminating anomalous vermin. Often used as a first-response team when tracking anomalous organisms. Have never lost an agent on any of their missions.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Lambda-12</td> <td>Kinkshamers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3101">SCP-3101</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2708">SCP-2708</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3999">SCP-3999</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/every-waking-hour-of-every-living-day">Every Breathing Minute of Every Waking Hour</a></td> <td>A task force dedicated to containing anomalies with which sexuality or sex/attraction are a main factor in effects.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces#lambda-14">MTF-Lambda-14</a></td> <td>One Star Reviewers</td> <td>See <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/task-forces">this page</a> for information about this particular task force.</td> <td>Previously only mentioned in passing by SCP-3999. Tasked with combating the Ambrose Restaurant minor GoI.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• STF-Lambda-17</td> <td>Presented in Color</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3462">SCP-3462</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Lambda-21</td> <td>Cave-Dwellers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1425">SCP-1425</a></td> <td>No description given.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Lambda-21</td> <td>Lake Monsters</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4850">SCP-4850</a></td> <td>Monitoring SCP-4850 pods.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MTF-Lambda-24</td> <td>Babysitters</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4714">SCP-4714</a></td> <td>Monitoring SCP-4714-A</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Lambda-30</td> <td>Sports Casting Performers</td> <td><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2206">SCP-2206</a></td> <td>SCP-specific task force.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>• MTF-Lambda-30</td> <td>Whiskey Tango Foxtrot</td> <td>