					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><strong>Note: These are different from the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/main">main</a> page's news and the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/archived-news">Archived News</a>. Those are for live updates on the site's workings, policies, and projects. This is a summary for site articles and fandom creations for the month in whole, posted at the beginning of each month. If you wish to comment on this news series as a whole, or make suggestions, please comment on this hub instead of the individual pages. Please do not add rating modules to any of the individual pages.</strong></p> </div> <hr /> <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <hr /> <div style="text-align: center;"> <h1><span>News for October 2020</span></h1> </div> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><strong>« <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-09-2020">September 2020</a> | <span style="text-decoration: underline;"><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-10-2020">October 2020</a></span> | <a class="newpage" href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-11-2020">November 2020</a> »</strong></p> </div> <p><span style="font-size:75%;">This is a series showing off news from the site, articles from the past month<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-273575-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup>, and fan-content for you to check out and discover! Be sure to leave a comment with your thoughts!</span></p> <h4><span>Fandom Stuff</span></h4> <ul> <li>SCP-FR (French language branch of the SCP Foundation) is running <a href="http://fondationscp.wikidot.com/le-concours-des-404-ans">a contest</a> for the SCP-404-FR slot. Participants are asked to write about &quot;An error, something that caused one or the consequences of one&quot;. The visual design of the contest hub is worth checking out whether you speak French or not.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-EN (English, this wiki) is conducting another <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/instagram-fan-art-contest-fall-2020">Instagram Fan Art Contest</a>.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-PL (Polish) is running the inventive <a href="http://scp-pl.wikidot.com/rezurekcja-usunietych">Resurrecting The Deleted</a> contest. Participants pick a title of a work from the Deletions Log, and write an article using said title.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-KO (Korean) finished its latest <a href="http://ko.scp-wiki.net/bimonthly-contests-2020#toc4">bimonthly contest</a>. The theme of the contest was &quot;Language&quot;.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-DE (German) concluded its second <a href="http://scp-wiki-de.wikidot.com/halloween-wettbewerb-2020">Halloween contest</a>.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-IT (Italian) also ran a <a href="http://fondazionescp.wikidot.com/concorso-halloween-2020-dr-zeno">Halloween contest</a> this month.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Featured Articles</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5380">SCP-5380</a> (by chiifu): My World [Featured by Truc Linh and Quadraginta]<br /> <em>As a result, the entire mall was showered with snowflakes and small paper hearts.</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-significant-others-part-a">The Significant Others, Part &quot;A&quot;</a> by HarryBlank [Featured by weizhong, Grigori Karpin, and PlaguePJP]<br /> <em>&quot;I'm not a subject in containment,&quot; said Phil.</em><br /> <em>Azad grinned. &quot;Sure you're not.&quot;</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/deer-and-the-overseers">Deer And The Overseers</a> <tt>[Deer College]</tt> by stormbreath [Featured by The Pighead, Marcelles_Raynes, and Pedagon]<br /> <em>In honor of the termination of the old Council, I'll be looking at the history of Deer's interactions with them…</em></li> </ul> <h4><span>Reviewer's Spotlight Articles</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5462">SCP-5462</a> (Misery is the State of Every Soul Burdened by Mortality.) by Cerastes [Selected by Cerastes]<br /> <em>[…] commonly referred to as his Black Paintings due to their emotionally disturbing contents, themes, and use of dark colours.</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5456">SCP-5456</a> (Sweatmother) by faminepulse [Selected by Grigori Karpin]<br /> <em>“We can be human, yeah we can be respectful, but we can't tolerate chaos. You</em> have <em>to be our<sup>[sic]</sup> own dads.”</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4423">SCP-4423</a> (StepDemon) by Dyslexion [Selected by Sonderance]<br /> <em>SCP-4423 is a Tartarean-Class demonic entity that manifests during sleep paralysis.</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5788">SCP-5788</a> (Partners in sync) by Riemann [Selected by OCuin]<br /> <em>The integration of SCP-5788 into the plumbing of the kitchen makes removal and characterisation difficult.</em></li> </ul> <div id="toc" class="floatright"> <div id="toc-action-bar"><a href="javascript:;" >Fold</a><a style="display: none" href="javascript:;" >Unfold</a></div> <div class="title">Table of Contents</div> <div id="toc-list"> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc0">Week of October 1st:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc1">Week of October 8th:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc2">Week of October 15th:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc3">Week of October 22nd:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc4">Fanart</a></div> </div> </div> <hr /> <p>You will notice little '📈' emojis beside some articles. That denotes SCP articles which were under 30 and tales which were under 20 when this edition of site news was posted. Give them a little love! Speaking from personal experience, the most frustrating thing that can happen to an article is not deletion, but stagnating below 20 without any comments. So try to read, vote, and comment on these articles! They're often hidden gems :)</p> <h3><span>Week of October 1st:</span></h3> <h4><span>SCPs</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5070">SCP-5070</a> (&quot;Man's (Only) Best Friend&quot;) - Desktop staplers are men's best friends. Written by Nickthebrick1.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5859">SCP-5859</a> (&quot;The PENTAGRAM Papers&quot;) - Your favorite good old-fashioned conspiracy, like the old days. You like it? Revealed by Anorrack.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5952">SCP-5952</a> (&quot;The Warbalang&quot;) - It rhymes with &quot;Trashwang&quot;. Not a strange animal discovered by UraniumEmpire, even if the name looks like that.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Tales</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/grape-flavored-cigars-and-funeral-pyres">Grape Flavored Cigars and Funeral Pyres</a> - &quot;<em>You know, I helped you out after last time, so I just need you to pass me your answer key…&quot;</em> Written by Iapetus The Acausal.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/kelipat">Kelipat Nogah</a> - &quot;<em>With the inclusion of Paraspecialists provided by the GOC and the CotBG, Xi-8 should now be able to handle most, if not all mid-level Sarkic Infestations.</em>&quot; Written by MalyceGraves.</li> </ul> <h4><span>GoI Formats</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/ambrose-three-portlands">Ambrose Three Portlands</a> - [Ambrose Restaurants] It's about time. Written by stormbreath.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/a-cosmic-cycle">A Cosmic Cycle</a> - [Arcadia] It's in a 8-bit setting, so it looks less impressive, but it will still be a cosmic cycle. Written by LillithHollyMisato.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Misc</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/uau102020">Underread and Underrated October 2020</a> - These challenges are, sure, worthy of you. Written by UraniumEmpire.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/granbozone">Granbo Zone</a> It's Edna Granbo's Author Page!</li> </ul> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <h3><span>Week of October 8th:</span></h3> <h4><span>SCPs</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="htt