st outside Potsdam. An old house is silent in Longmont. The sky shines, and the night moves on. Radio towers call over great distances; computers flash in the dimming rays of the sun. Nobody can remember them all.</em>&quot; Written by Tufto.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Misc</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/artpage-fartpage">lynch artpage fartpage</a> -It's stephlynch's art page!</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/interviewing-icons-ihp">Interviewing Icons - Ihp</a> - Ihp, creator of S&amp;C Plastics and many othr things, as interviewed by WhiteGuard.</li> </ul> <h3><span>Week of October 22nd:</span></h3> <h4><span>SCPs</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5240">SCP-5240</a> (&quot;Vergussenheit, the City of the Forgotten&quot;) - About what I said above, we don't have to worry anymore. They finally found a place. Builded by LanceRadioactive.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5464">SCP-5464</a> (&quot;The responsibility we bear&quot;) - We will need to bear something that is not a bear. Handled by Ralliston.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5221">SCP-5221</a> (&quot;&quot;The Day After Tomorrow&quot;&quot;) - You know, you can say &quot;in 2 days&quot;, no need to be so melodramatic. Written by chiifu.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5924">SCP-5924</a> (&quot;Professional Attachment&quot;) - It was supposed to be forbidden. Written by Blightknell.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5680">SCP-5680</a> (&quot;The Bird Factory&quot;) - Team RR stole the spotlight for a while, but Team Bird is still here, not quite dying. Written by not_a_seagull.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5124">SCP-5124</a> (&quot;playdo mous&quot;) - the mous like in this book by the man sir art spee ghel mann but you can play wif it it's J Dune who made that talk to him.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5762">SCP-5762</a> (&quot;a doctor a day&quot;) - #1Day1DoctorDecember. Written by Rounderhouse.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5268">SCP-5268</a> (&quot;Off the Wall Taste&quot;) - The taste is so good and so strong, all the walls can explode because of that. Even what's over the garden walls. Written by ghosterposter.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5119">SCP-5119</a> (&quot;Uncle Charlie's Toys and Games&quot;) - There's people who miss the first days of companies like Wondertainment, when it was just a little, small company. Uncle Charlie is one of those people. Written by J Dune.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5502">SCP-5502</a> (&quot;Go for the gold.&quot;) - If you want to have that, don't forget : there's a flow. Go with the flow and ask yourself this question : do I believe it in my head? Dug by Alb123.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Tales</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/chapter-5-pre-partum-anxieties">Pre-Partum Anxieties</a> - &quot;<em>Uh… doesn't this… faze you at all? What's happening in the town?</em>&quot; Written by Ihp.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/do-you-like-huey-lewis-and-the-news">Do you like Huey Lewis and the News?</a> - &quot;<em>Food Fact: Consuming human brains can lead to Kuru, but not if you're very careful!</em>&quot; Written by Rounderhouse.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/tangled-web">Tangled Web</a> - &quot;<em>They silently sat there looking over the frozen field. Carlotta heard an owl hooting in the distant woods a few hundred meters away. Otherwise, it was very quiet.</em>&quot; Written by Grigori Karpin.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/what-if-things-don-t-make-sense">What If Things Don't Make Sense?</a> - &quot;<em>But when I looked at the lawn, the grass was purple.</em>&quot; Written by DarkStuff.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/a-terrible-thing">A Terrible Thing</a> - &quot;<em>The jailer steps out into the cold. She is well insulated but it is not long before rimefrost begins to creep along the emerald edges of her vision. She does not seem to mind.</em>&quot; Written by Riemann.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/omens">Omens</a> - &quot;<em>They had come to this shore to die, and in telling us, offer the chance to live.</em>&quot; Written by DodoDevil.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/isolated-efficient">Isolated, Efficient.</a> - &quot;<em>Glacon drops his personality core into the void, watching it fall until it is too small to see.</em>&quot; Written by Tyumen.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/acroamatic-abatement">Everything You Need to Know About Acroamatic Abatement But Were Too Confused by the Name to Ask</a> - &quot;<em>One final point: &quot;acroamatic&quot; means &quot;esoteric.&quot; I could have told you that right at the start, but, well, you might not have read the rest.</em>&quot; Written by HarryBlank.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/dead-dogs-magic-mounties">Dead Dogs, Magic Mounties</a> - &quot;<em>With a permanent home for the researchers employed by CLIO-4 and the AAG now secure, both organizations were dissolved and new Operational Sections took their place.</em>&quot; Written by HarryBlank.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/shut-it-down">Shut It Down</a> - &quot;<em>Someone should probably call Light.</em>&quot; Written by Grigori Karpin.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/when-its-all-over">When It's All Over</a> - &quot;<em>They panic for a moment, moving around and trembling at the sight of the beast. It doesn't bother with them.</em>&quot; Written by stormbreath.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/chapter-4-nobody-prays-for-february">Nobody Prays For February</a> - &quot;// Allison heard the elevator to the surface ding, open, and then shut. She was left in a dimly-lit infirmary, alone but for the patients in the beds.<em>&quot; Written by Ihp.</em></li> <li><em><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/lilies">Lilies</a> - &quot;</em>Eighteen days later, as both Kyōko and Yuriko met over drinks, neither quite 